Notebook[{Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["wilsonLoop", "ObjectName"], Cell[TextData[{Cell["   ", "ModInfo"], Cell[BoxData["wilsonLoop[h,wcc,occ,start,end]"], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "computes Wilson-loop eigenphases for an isolated occupied subspace along a forward reciprocal-lattice loop."}], "Usage"], Cell["start and end have the same coordinate dimension and end-start must be 2 Pi times an integer reciprocal vector. wcc contains one fractional orbital center per Hamiltonian basis state.", "Notes"], Cell["Occupied-subspace overlaps are unitarized by SVD and the endpoint is closed by the orbital-center sewing matrix. The production calculation does not use an eigenvector-gauge fallback.", "Notes"], Cell["The default return is a sorted list of phases divided by Pi. Alternate outputs expose Wannier centers modulo one, Wilson eigenvalues, or a diagnostic Association.", "Notes"], Cell["wilsonLoop returns $Failed and issues a message when the loop is not reciprocal-lattice closed, centers/occupation are inconsistent, H is non-Hermitian, the direct gap closes, endpoint covariance fails, an overlap is singular, or an option is invalid. It does not repair the input or switch to an approximate fallback.", "Notes"], Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon"], "\"PathSubdivisions\"", "50", Cell["Positive number of equal forward-path intervals.", "TableText"]}, {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon"], "\"HermitianTolerance\"", "10^-10", Cell["Nonnegative Hermiticity and final unitarity tolerance.", "TableText"]}, {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon"], "\"GapTolerance\"", "10^-9", Cell["Nonnegative minimum direct-gap threshold for an occupied subspace smaller than the full Hilbert space.", "TableText"]}, {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon"], "\"CovarianceTolerance\"", "10^-8", Cell["Nonnegative endpoint sewing-covariance tolerance.", "TableText"]}, {Cell["      ", "TableRowIcon"], "\"OverlapTolerance\"", "10^-10", Cell["Nonnegative lower bound for link singular values.", "TableText"]}, {Cell